WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.412
Here are the program's own rules, and
most of them are labeled design guidance.

2
00:00:04.412 --> 00:00:08.797
New apps can't use secrets, and their
certificates are capped at a hundred and

3
00:00:08.797 --> 00:00:11.373
eighty days, set on both
object types because

4
00:00:11.373 --> 00:00:13.600
the admin center expects them to match.

5
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.991
An app that truly can't use a certificate

6
00:00:15.991 --> 00:00:18.600
gets a time-limited
exception with a record.

7
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.962
Older apps get a year while they're fixed.

8
00:00:20.962 --> 00:00:23.612
Every registered app
gets the property lock.

9
00:00:23.612 --> 00:00:25.438
No extra license is needed.

10
00:00:25.438 --> 00:00:29.120
And rotation joins Key Vault,
which can renew a certificate,

11
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.640
to the app registration, which
renews nothing on its own.
